<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vic-sur-Seille</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vic-sur-Seille is a small town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a>, north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Its salt works enriched the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metz">Metz</a>, who made it their residence after the citizens of Metz won independence in the 13th century. The painter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georges-de-la-tour">Georges de La Tour</a> was born there in 1593.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vic-sur-seille.jpg" alt="Vic-sur-Seille" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Ske assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Placevicsseille2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
